# I’ll remove the _Check for payment problems/Bolt Balance_ drop-downs. Good to know that it’s happening automatically now. 
# I’ve edited step 3 as specified below, please check:

{color:#6554c0}*Step 3: Archive the user's account*{color}

* {color:#6554c0}Let the user know that we will proceed with their request and ask them to log out from their app{color}
* {color:#6554c0}Click on the {color}{color:#6554c0}_User archival_{color}{color:#6554c0} tab{color}
* {color:#6554c0}Copy the Zendesk/Beehive ticket link with the request and paste it to {color}{color:#6554c0}_Zendesk ticket field_{color}
* {color:#6554c0}Click on the {color}{color:#6554c0}_Archive_ {color}{color:#6554c0}button{color}
* {color:#6554c0}If the account cannot be archived, the system will let you know by showing an error message in Admin. It is REQUIRED that the CS agent informs the user requesting the deletion that the account cannot be archived and why:{color}
** {color:#6554c0}_unpaid_orders_{color}{color:#6554c0}: the user has debt (negative balance) or failed payments in countries that do not have Bolt Balance (HU, AT). The user should top up their balance in the app or (in HU, AT) retry the payment.{color}
** {color:#6554c0}_ongoing_orders_{color}{color:#6554c0}: the user has a pending payment associated with a recent order. It's possible that the user has an active order or the recent order wasn't captured yet. Put the ticket on-hold and try again in 24 hours. If you still receive the same error, submit a ticket to the Fraud team via {color}[{color:#6554c0}Service Desk.{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/3/group/-1]{color:#6554c0} {color}
** {color:#6554c0}_chargeback_payments_{color}{color:#6554c0}/{color}{color:#6554c0}_payment_problems_{color}{color:#6554c0}: the amount of chargebacks exceeds the amount we allow. {color}
** {color:#6554c0}_same_phone_number_many_accounts_{color}{color:#6554c0}: in the last 6 months, the user has had multiple accounts under the same phone number. {color}

By the way, we can mention all those reasons to the users, right (as they should know why we’re not proceeding with their account deletion)? If yes, to what extent (e.g. can the user know that they shouldn’t have multiple accounts associated with the same phone number during a 6 month period or the timeframe shouldn’t be specified)? 

You also mentioned privacy policy: could you please let me know where exactly the user can find information about chargebacks + the fact that they’re not allowed to have many accounts with the same number (during the 6 month period)? I checked our global terms of service for passengers + global privacy notice for passengers but didn’t find this information.

Looking forward to hearing from you,

Eliise

