{color:#333333}Answers in blue:{color}

{color:#333333}Not familiar myself with the kitchen side of FB ads. How is the FB lead form built up?{color} {color:#0000ff}It's basically a pop up that opens up when someone clicks on the ad. The pop up asks for your name, @ address and number. There is an option to add T&C's to the pop up. More details here:{color} [https://www.facebook.com/business/help/397336587121938?id=735435806665862|https://www.facebook.com/business/help/397336587121938?id=735435806665862]{color:#0000ff}{color} {color:#333333}This is in the FB environment and details are received by Bolt, we will be the ones forwarding the contact details (i.e. personal details) to Eternis? So Eternis is actually not part of the entire deal between FB and Bolt?{color} {color:#0000ff}Eternis's FB page is linked to the ads, so they are Eternis-branded. We can also add a note to the T&Cs, but what the user sees is an Eternis ad.{color}

{color:#333333}Eternis has the option to contact the leads but not an obligation?{color} {color:#0000ff}Correct{color} {color:#333333}I am{color}{color:#333333} just brainstorming here, to what extent we want to have an agreement between Bolt and Eternis, in order for it not to be an overkill.{color} {color:#0000ff}Yes,{color} [@Paweł Pyrlik|mailto:pawel.pyrlik@bolt.eu]{color:#0000ff} I would like a guarantee from Eternis that they will process the leads and assign them to Bolt unless the driver specifically requests otherwise. Do you agree?{color}

{color:#333333}If my understanding above is correct, whichever T&C Bolt consents with for the leads, we need to make sure we do not violate GDPR laws and the persons contacting give their consent for their personal info to be shared with third parties (i.e. Eternis).{color} [https://www.facebook.com/business/direct_terms_ads_en.php|https://www.facebook.com/business/direct_terms_ads_en.php]{color:#333333} 3.5 covers it, in my view, but{color} [{color:#333333}Adriana Sokólska{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61b0698dfe9f3000680f0585]{color:#333333} to confirm.{color} {color:#0000ff}Hopefully the FB Leadform T&C's protects us from it? Normally the user gets T&C's once they land onto the Driver Portal (we give their details to fleets). So we need a similar T&C in the FB leadform.{color}

{color:#333333}Also,{color} [{color:#333333}Adriana Sokólska{color}|https://taxify.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61b0698dfe9f3000680f0585]{color:#333333} should the ad itself be specific in a way, so potential leads understand that their details will be shared with one specific fleet who will then contact them?{color} {color:#0000ff}The trick here is, the ad is run by us but it's branded with Eternis. So people might not know it's Bolt paying for the ads. Is that a problem?{color}

