Hi,

from privacy perspective, this requires market-by-market analysis, as there might regulatory obligations in place requiring us to keep certain data for compliance purposes, in particular stemming from tax and accounting-related legislation. 

In principle, when we are ceasing the operations and looking to delete the data, the following actions should be taken into consideration prior to deleting the data:

* indication what market is in scope;
* mapping the data in scope;
* analysis by finance and tax teams to determine finance-related requirements;
* analysis by the legal and privacy team on other local requirements relating to the data retention;
* based on legal and finance analysis we can then determine the data that could be immediately deleted and setting up the retention schedule for other data set that may be covered by longer retention requirements.

BR,

Adriana

