Please review the changes in the [glossary|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/LEG/pages/3655762229/The+High+Priority+Tools+Complex+Workflow]. To summarise, the list of Case Statuses for the UK and IE will be as follows:

* *Driver/Rider needs a callback:* The report is not clear and we have to call the user back to receive additional information;
* *Waiting for clearance letter:* We have asked the user to send us a clearance letter from the police showing that they do not have any criminal charges before they can get unblocked;
* *Accused party contacted:* We have contacted the reported user for additional information;
* *Determining HP:* We have contacted the reporting and/or reported user for additional information to determine whether this case is a safety issue;
* *Future block:* We have placed a future block (in 6h) on the driver’s account;
* *Future block 2nd check:* We have placed a future block (in 6h) on the driver’s account and should contact the driver right before the block goes on to check whether they have responded to us.
* *Pending stakeholder review (only in the Investigation Tool):* We wish to conclude the case by unblocking the reported user in case of serious allegations and we are waiting for the approval from the UK/IE stakeholders.

