Hi [~accountid:618d2fe286c210006aa6241e] , [~accountid:61445ecbe057c6006a5163cc] ,

from privacy perspective this is not expected role allocation in this scenario. Please see the risks below: 

* Controller-to-processor data flows means that Bolt will be processing data on behalf of the agency and in accordance with the instructions of the original data controller, so if requested, we might be obliged to introduce specific safeguards to our set up to accommodate this;
* Under the agreement, the agency will have the right to audit Bolt (in its processor’s capacity) and review our internal set up;
* In case of a data breach relating to picker’s data, Bolt might be exposed not only to the regulatory proceeding (as it would still be the case for controller-to-controller data transfer), but also can be facing liability towards the agency.

Ultimately this is a business decision, but this set up is not aligned with our standard for this type of arrangements.

Best,

Adriana

